header><h1>Shortest Transformation Sequence</h1></header><div class=3D"styl=
e_problemDescription__T4cPe"><p>Given two words, <code>start</code> and <co=
de>end</code>, and a dictionary containing an array of words, return the <s=
trong>length of the shortest transformation sequence</strong> to transform =
start to end. A transformation sequence is a series of words in which:</p><=
ul>
<li>Each word differs from the preceding word by exactly one letter.</li>
<li>Each word in the sequence exists in the dictionary.</li>
</ul><p>If no such transformation sequence exists, return 0.</p><h4 id=3D"e=
xample">Example:</h4><pre><code class=3D"hljs language-python">Input: start=
 =3D <span class=3D"hljs-string">'red'</span>, end =3D <span class=3D"hljs-=
string">'hit'</span>,
       dictionary =3D [
            <span class=3D"hljs-string">'red'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-s=
tring">'bed'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'hat'</span>, <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">'rod'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'rad'</span>, <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-string">'rat'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'hit'</=
span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">'bad'</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string=
">'bat'</span>
       ]
Output: <span class=3D"hljs-number">5</span>
</code></pre><h3 id=3D"constraints">Constraints:</h3><ul>
<li>All words are the same length.</li>
<li>All words contain only lowercase English letters.</li>
<li>The dictionary contains no duplicate words.</li>
</ul></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>In a transformation sequence, each transformation involves changing one =
letter of a word to get another word. Consider the following example:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
