enting a node in the graph.  The value associated with each key is a list o=
f strings, also enclosed in square brackets, representing the nodes directl=
y connected to the key node (its neighbors). For instance, 'red': [ 'bed', =
'rad', 'rod'] indicates that the node 'red' is connected to nodes 'bed', 'r=
ad', and 'rod'.  Similarly, 'bed' connects to 'red' and 'bad', 'hat' connec=
ts to 'rat', 'bat', and 'hit', and 'hit' connects only to 'hat'.  The ellip=
